{
  "_meta": {
    "purpose": "Structured move effects, scripted behaviors, template passives, rotations, and compound-fight unit templates for the WHOLE bestiary, transcribed from off-campaign-bestiary.json fx/special strings and docs/off-restat-worksheet.md. Scripted triggers auto-fire for AI-controlled instances only; for GM-piloted instances they surface as prompts and never act uninvoked. The GM's hand is never gated: any trigger fires from the console regardless of condition. Anything not expressible here surfaces to the GM as a resolve-by-hand prompt — never half-built.",
    "vocabulary": {
      "moveEffects": "status | statuses[] | statChange | drainCp[lo,hi] | hits | cpCost | lifesteal | selfDamage | selfHeal | selfHealPctMax | selfRandomElement | healAlly{amount,cureStatus} | allyStatChange | allyStatus | allyCureAll | allyStripDown | plusCurrentHpPct | ignoresDef | forceElement | randomElement | attackElementOwnWeakness | attackElementBestVsTarget | setElementRandom | summon{name,count,realCount} | availableBelowHpPct | formOnly[] | oncePerFight | scripted",
      "triggers.when": "turn | hpPctLte | orTurn | everySeconds (repeating) | allyDied | watchAgeGte (repeating while a watch mark exists)",
      "triggers.action": "summon | selfStatus | statChanges[] | selfHealBonus | setForm | castMove | blast | partyStatus | mark | resolveWatch | addMove | addMoveEffect | announce | flee | forfeitDrop | die",
      "passives": "selfHealPerAction | purification | sacredMission | chainMastery"
    },
    "flags": [
      "Gilles de Rais's optional 2008 martial-check trait is dropped, per its own data note ('drop if schema purity wins').",
      "Enoch's Double Attack 'frequency rises below 60%' conflicts with the uniform-random AI rule; uniform stands — pilot him below 60% if you want the canon cadence.",
      "Critic-burnt's HELP self-buffs 'ESP/DEF/AGI'; ESP is not a stat-change type in the system, so the buffs land as ATK/DEF/AGI Up.",
      "Pastel-burnt's sequential head spawns (~every 18s) and kill-heads-kills-body win condition are GM-assembled from the unit templates below (waves + manual spawns + Players-panel edits); the timing hand is yours.",
      "Carnival's four Games and the bidirectional prize-tempo system are GM-run: the moves below all resolve, Game transitions announce at 75/50/25%, but phase move-pools and prize gauge-fills are your calls (pilot him).",
      "Ballman's set-piece minigame is a GM call per canon; straight-fodder stats work as data."
    ]
  },
